# --- Hardware/CAD scratch ---
*.f3z.backup
*.bak
*.tmp
# ad-hoc exploded view of the HAA joint, kept locally. Imports the servo mesh
# by absolute path, so it is machine-specific as written — see cad_assets and
# leg_v6/preview_leg_assembly.scad for the portable form if it ever ships.
hardware/cad/leg_v6/exploded_haa.scad

# --- KiCad ---
# per-user GUI state (window layout, last sheet)
*.kicad_prl
# KiCad auto-backup archives
*-backups/
# regenerated footprint cache
fp-info-cache
# in-progress autosaves
_autosave-*
# editor lock files (pcbnew/eeschema open)
*.lck
# exported DRC/ERC reports (regenerable)
*.drc.json
*.erc.json
*-drc.rpt
*-erc.rpt
hardware/cad/chassis/jetson_case_ref.stl.orig

# graphify knowledge-graph tooling output (scratch)
graphify-out/

# SDD controller scratch (subagent-driven-development ledger) — not repo content
.superpowers/

# stderr-redirect scratch files from sim training/eval runs
sim/nova_mjx/*.err

# Assembly-preview STLs — build artifacts, not source. `preview_assembly.py`
# rebuilds both in ~2s from the part STLs, and trimesh output is not
# byte-stable, so tracking them meant a dirty tree after every rebuild (and a
# custom merge driver to stop the binary 3-way merges conflicting).
hardware/cad/chassis/chassis_assembly_preview.stl
hardware/cad/chassis/foot_assembly_preview.stl
hardware/cad/leg_v6/leg_v6_assembly_preview.stl

# Render-only 3D models kept on disk but deliberately NOT committed (#201):
# ~31 MB that no board file references — the unused alternates named in
# 3dmodels/README.md. The four models the v6 boards actually point at ARE
# tracked. Delete these ignores if a board is ever repointed at one.
hardware/pcb-mods/3dmodels/Teensy_4.1_Assembly.STEP
hardware/pcb-mods/3dmodels/arduino_nano_esp32.step
hardware/pcb-mods/3dmodels/arduino_nano_r4.step

# Trained sim policies are INPUTS downloaded from Colab/Drive, not repo outputs —
# see sim/nova_mjx/artifacts/policies/README.md. Binaries stay out; the README
# that says what to drop there is tracked.
sim/nova_mjx/artifacts/policies/*
!sim/nova_mjx/artifacts/policies/README.md

# HFE mouth-study fit coupon (#221) — NOT a robot part. Regenerated in seconds
# by hardware/cad/leg_v6/hfe_mouth_study.py from the gate-fresh STLs; committing
# it would need a freshness gate for a throwaway coupon. The script is the record.
hardware/cad/leg_v6/coax_hfe_mouth_coupon.stl

# sliced G-code — derived, regenerable from slice_plate.py; the RECORD (docs/print-records) is what we keep
hardware/cad/slices/

# per-worktree verification evidence (tools/verify) — never shared
.verify-log
